# Graphify (graph first, grep last)

This repo has a local, code-only knowledge graph at `graphify-out/` (rebuilt by `graphify update .`; not committed).

**Default order for every code question:**

1. **Graph** — `graphify explain`, `graphify path`, or `graphify query` (see skill `graphify-code-nav`).
2. **Open only the lines** the graph returns — never whole files by default.
3. **Grep last** — only for exact literals the graph cannot answer (error string, CSS id, env var name).

**Keep the graph fresh:** run `graphify update .` after editing code and before an audit. Local clones may also run `graphify hook install` so updates happen on commit.

**Before changing a shared function:** `graphify explain "<symbol>"` and list every caller in the PR **Regression audit** section. Do not edit shared helpers without that caller check.

This applies to you and to every subagent that explores code. Include this rule in subagent prompts. Do not skip the graph because files are "already known".

Only skip graphify when `graphify-out/graph.json` does not exist yet — then run `graphify update .` first.
